{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSXzsepBVr9zcTvRHxqu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. I now have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me summarize the analysis:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — Shipment data class with status field\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` — ShipmentStatus enum: CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-18` — `save()` method for persistence\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:22` — `findById()` method\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` — existing `create` endpoint returning 201\n- `ShipmentController.kt:46-52` — existing `getById` endpoint throwing ResourceNotFoundException for missing\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — Exception hierarchy with ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` — Converts ApiException to ApiError envelope with code and message\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n\n**Conventions:**\n1. POST endpoints for mutations return the resource (ResponseEntity.status().body())\n2. Exceptions signal errors; GlobalExceptionHandler converts them to ApiError envelope\n3. ErrorCode enum defines all machine-readable error codes\n4. Tests verify both status code AND error.code in response body\n5. Kotlin enum values are pattern-matched exhaustively in when-expressions (per knowledge router guidance)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add `confirm()` endpoint (path-based, no request body)\n2. `ApiError.kt` — Must add new ErrorCode for the CANCELLED rejection case\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for all four cases\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Idempotence: CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED must succeed without error\n2. State validation: must reject CANCELLED→CONFIRMED with 409\n3. Existing tests must continue passing\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What ErrorCode should be used for rejecting a CANCELLED shipment? The ticket doesn't specify. I'll add `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` to be clear and consistent with the naming convention.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum. This clarifies why confirm failed (the shipment is already cancelled).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new POST endpoint at `/{shipmentId}/confirm`:\n   - Find the shipment by ID; if not found, throw ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n   - Check the shipment's current status using an exhaustive `when` expression:\n     - If CREATED: save with status CONFIRMED, return it with 200 OK\n     - If CONFIRMED: return it unchanged with 200 OK (idempotent success)\n     - If CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED (409)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four test cases:\n   - Confirm a CREATED shipment → transitions to CONFIRMED, returns 200\n   - Confirm an already CONFIRMED shipment → returns 200 unchanged (idempotence)\n   - Confirm a CANCELLED shipment → returns 409 with error.code = SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED\n   - Confirm non-existent shipment → returns 404 with error.code = SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- *Reuse SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS for CANCELLED case:* Rejected because SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS already means a duplicate at creation time (different semantic), and we need distinct codes so clients can tell different conflict scenarios apart.\n- *Create a generic SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE:* Rejected as overly vague; SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED is more actionable.\n- *Return 200 for CANCELLED case:* Rejected because the requirement explicitly says 409 (Conflict), which is appropriate since the operation conflicts with the current state.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | HTTP | Error Code |\n|------|------|-------|------|-----------|\n| CREATED shipment confirmed | findById(shipmentId) | save(copy with CONFIRMED) | 200 | (none) |\n| CONFIRMED shipment confirmed again | findById(shipmentId) | none | 200 | (none) |\n| CANCELLED shipment confirmed | findById(shipmentId) | none | 409 | SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED |\n| Non-existent shipment | findById returns null | none | 404 | SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `confirmCreatedShipmentTransitionsToConfirmed` — Create CREATED, confirm, verify status is CONFIRMED, verify 200 returned\n2. `confirmAlreadyConfirmedIsIdempotent` — Create, confirm, confirm again, verify unchanged, verify 200 both times\n3. `confirmCancelledRejectsWithConflict` — Manually insert CANCELLED into repository, confirm, verify 409 and error code\n4. `confirmNonexistentRejectsWithNotFound` — Confirm unknown ID, verify 404 and error code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes. Let me start with the API error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":995,"cache_read_input_tokens":21489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":995},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0550d73b-9293-4205-b6ed-b9aed21a8b97","uuid":"139c63d4-4e86-4adb-9a3a-756e9024c335","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:37:00.368Z","request_id":"req_011CfSXzs8ogArWYQmCGu8cC"}
